cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these resources in a course, a talk or a paper, please cite them as below."
title: "Optimization in Action: interactive operations research resources"
abstract: >-
  An open library of interactive operations research examples in five levels (linear, integer,
  mixed-integer and nonlinear programming, and other operations research methods) that run in the
  browser, in English, Spanish, Portuguese and French, plus four applied research cases from Colombia.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Pesca
    given-names: Jaime
    website: "https://jaimepesca.com"
url: "https://learn-optimization.jaimepesca.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/JaimePesca/Educational_Resources_Optimization"
keywords:
  - operations research
  - optimization
  - linear programming
  - integer programming
  - mixed-integer programming
  - nonlinear programming
  - teaching resources
  - interactive simulations
